# Every page is served at its address without ".html" (/who-we-are,
# /work/denver). Asked for the .html address, Cloudflare redirects on its own,
# but with a 307 — a temporary redirect, which tells Google to keep the .html
# URL in its index instead of the one the site actually serves. These rules
# make the move permanent. They run before asset matching, so they win over
# that built-in 307.
#
# A new page needs a line here, and its canonical, og:url, JSON-LD url and
# sitemap entry written without ".html" too.

/index.html                    /                         301
/who-we-are.html               /who-we-are               301
/work/bbhhomes.html            /work/bbhhomes            301
/work/denver.html              /work/denver              301
/work/fig.html                 /work/fig                 301
/work/getmyrugs.html           /work/getmyrugs           301
/work/parmandesigns.html       /work/parmandesigns       301
/work/prakshi.html             /work/prakshi             301
/work/tenderheartschool.html   /work/tenderheartschool   301
